ted install also keeps each importer whose dependencies"," /// `hoisted_prior`, the previous install's current lockfile, records, as long","-/// as the wanted `lockfile` still has that importer. An importer no install","-/// materialized a dependency for stays out, so the selection still decides","-/// what a first install brings in.","+/// as the wanted `lockfile` still has that importer and the project is present","+/// on disk (`real_importer_ids`). An importer no install materialized a","+/// dependency for, or whose project is missing from disk, stays out."," ///"," /// Pass `hoisted_prior` only for a hoisted layout. Other layouts give each"," /// importer its own `node_modules`, so the selection alone is complete."," pub(crate) fn selected_materialization_ids(","     lockfile: &Lockfile,","     selected: &HashSet<String>,","+    real_importer_ids: Option<&HashSet<String>>,","     hoisted_prior: Option<&Lockfile>,"," ) -> HashSet<String> {","     let previously_materialized = hoisted_prior","         .into_iter()","         .flat_map(|prior| &prior.importers)","         .filter(|(importer_id, snapshot)| {","-            records_a_dependency(snapshot) && lockfile.importers.contains_key(*importer_id)","+            records_a_dependency(snapshot)","+                && lockfile.importers.contains_key(*importer_id)","+                && real_importer_ids.is_none_or(|real| real.contains(*importer_id))","         })","         .map(|(importer_id, _)| importer_id);","     selected","@@ -36,11 +39,13 @@ pub(crate) fn selected_materialization_ids("," ///"," /// Applies `groups` (`--prod`, `--dev`, `--no-optional`) to `selected` and"," /// any importers reached from `selected`, while preserving the dependency","-/// groups `hoisted_prior` already materialized for unselected importers.","+/// groups `hoisted_prior` already materialized for unselected importers that","+/// are present on disk (`real_importer_ids`)."," pub(crate) fn selected_materialization_closure(","     l